  "notes": "{再編|さいへん} refers to fundamentally reorganizing the structure of an organization, system, or political landscape. It implies more substantial change than minor adjustments.\n\nFORMS:\n{再|さい} (again, re-) + {編|へん} (compose, organize).\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {組織|そしき}{再編|さいへん}: organizational restructuring\n- {事業|じぎょう}{再編|さいへん}: business restructuring\n- {政界|せいかい}{再編|さいへん}: political realignment\n- {再編|さいへん}{計画|けいかく}: restructuring plan\n- {再編|さいへん}を{行|おこな}う: to carry out restructuring\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {改編|かいへん}: reorganization (similar but often smaller-scale)\n- {統廃合|とうはいごう}: consolidation and merger (combining and closing)\n- {改革|かいかく}: reform (broader, can include policy changes)\n- リストラ: restructuring (loanword, often implies layoffs)",
